entions that after 24 hours, more nurses visited. If it takes longer than 24 hours for symptoms to appear, then the decrease in humidity would cause the delay in visiting. But I'm not sure if this is the assumption.\n\nD) At least some of the visits to the school nurse after the system was modified were due to illness.\nThis seems like a direct assumption. Because if the decrease in humidity caused more visits, then at least some of those visits were due to illness. This would support the conclusion that humidity caused illness.\n\nSo, the argument likely states that because of the decrease in humidity, more nurses visited, implying that the decrease caused illness. Therefore, the assumption is that at least some of the visits after the system was modified were due to illness.\n\nLooking back at the options, D seems to be the correct answer because it directly supports the conclusion that the decrease in humidity caused more visits, implying illness.\n</think>\n\nThe argument assumes that at least some of the visits to the school nurse after the system was modified were due to illness. This supports the conclusion that decreased humidity caused more visits, implying illness.\n\n**Answer: D**",
