wo project team members, including the moderator.\" So perhaps the project team can have the moderator plus one more person, making two people total. So the possible team sizes are either one person (moderator only) or two people (moderator plus one member). But the options given are combinations of two people, so perhaps the team includes the moderator and one more person.\n\nBut let's focus on the statements first.\n\nLet's consider each statement and see what they imply.\n\nStarting with Yan Zi's statement: If I become the host, I will invite Zeng Yin or Xun Chen as members. So if Yan Zi is the host, then either Zeng Yin or Xun Chen must be on the team. Alternatively, if Yan Zi is not the host, this statement doesn't impose any condition.\n\nZeng Yin's statement: If I become the host, I will invite Yan Zi or Meng Shen. So if Zeng Yin is the host, then either Yan Zi or Meng Shen must be on the team.\n\nXun Chen's statement: I can be the host only if Yan Zi becomes a member. So this is a conditional statement: If Xun Chen is the host, then Yan Zi must be on the team. Alternatively, if Xun Chen is not the host, this statement doesn't impose any condition.\n\nMeng Shen's statement: I can become the host only if Xun Chen or Yan Zi becomes a member. So if Meng Shen is the host, then either Xun Chen or Yan Zi must be on the team. Alternatively, if Meng Shen is not the host, this doesn't impose any condition.\n\nNow, let's consider the possible moders. The moderator can be any of the four, but let's see which ones are possible.\n\nFirst, let's consider each possible moderator and see what the team can be.\n\nCase 1: Yan Zi is the moderator.\n\nIf Yan Zi is the moderator, then according to his statement, he will invite Zeng Yin or Xun Chen. So the team would include Yan Zi and either Zeng Yin or Xun Chen. But since the team can have up to two members (moderator plus one more), the team would be either Yan Zi and Zeng Yin or Yan Zi and Xun Chen.\n\nBut let's check the other statements to see if this is consistent.\n\nIf Yan Zi is the moderator, then according to his statement, he invites Zeng Yin or Xun Chen. Now, let's look at Zeng Yin's statement. If Zeng Yin is the host, then she would invite Yan Zi or Meng Shen. But in this case, Yan Zi is the moderator, not Zeng Yin. So Zeng Yin's statement doesn't apply here because she isn't the host. Similarly, Xun Chen's statement: if Xun Chen is the host, then Yan Zi must be on the team. But in this case, Yan Zi is the moderator, not Xun Chen. So Xun Chen's statement doesn't apply.\n\nMeng Shen's statement: if she is the host, then Xun Chen or Yan Zi must be on the team. But in this case, Yan Zi is the moderator, not the host. So if she is the host, she would need Xun Chen or Yan Zi, but since Yan Zi is the moderator, she would need Xun Chen. But if she is the host, she would invite someone else, but according to her statement, she can become the host only if Xun Chen or Yan Zi. Since Yan Zi is already on the team, this is okay.\n\nBut let's see if the team can include both Yan Zi and someone else. If Yan Zi is the moderator, and he invites Zeng Yin, then the team would be Yan Zi and Zeng Yin. Alternatively, if he invites Xun Chen, the team would be Yan Zi and Xun Chen.\n\nNow, let's check if these are consistent with the other statements.\n\nIf the team is Yan Zi and Zeng Yin, then Zeng Yin's statement: if she is the host, she would invite Yan Zi or Meng Shen. But in this case, Zeng Yin is not the host, so her statement doesn't apply. However, if Zeng Yin is on the team, does that affect anything? Let's see.\n\nAlternatively, if the team is Yan Zi and Xun Chen, then Xun Chen's statement: if he is the host, then Yan Zi must be on the team. But in this case, Xun Chen is not the host, so his statement doesn't apply. However, if Xun Chen is on the team, does that affect anything?\n\nWait, perhaps I'm getting ahead of myself. Let's consider each possible combination and see if they are possible