he supervisor agreed with that part.\n\nD) Whether closed furnaces are more fuel-efficient. The supervisor's disagreement is about this point.\n\nSo the question is asking which point the supervisor is disagreeing with. The supervisor agreed with the manager's conclusion that the new process will cost more but disagreed that the new furnaces are more fuel-efficient. Therefore, the point the supervisor is disagreeing with is D) Whether closed copper-smelting furnaces are more fuel-efficient than open furnaces.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. The manager's point was about the cost of running the new process, which the supervisor agreed with. The supervisor's disagreement is about the fuel efficiency of the new furnaces. So the question is about which point the supervisor is disagreeing with, which is D.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the question is about the point the manager made that the new process reduces sulfur dioxide, but the supervisor is disagreeing with that point. However, the question is specifically about the supervisor's disagreement, which is about fuel efficiency.\n\nSo the correct answer should be D.\n</think>\n\nThe supervisor's disagreement is about whether the new furnaces are more fuel-efficient. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Whether closed copper-smelting furnaces are more fuel-efficient than open furnaces.",
