roduct. So, looking at the options, D directly states the consequence of repeated ads causing boredom and anger, which is a strong point of the argument.\n\nOption C is also relevant but perhaps more about the diversity of audiences rather than the consequence of the ad. Option A is about viewers' feelings, but it's not as direct as D.\n\nSo, the best option is D because it clearly states the negative effect of repeated ads, which is the main point of the argument.\n</think>\n\nThe best option that emphasizes the argument is:\n\n**D) Repeated playback of the same ad will cause tv viewers to get bored or even angry, and thus have a strong antipathy to the products that the merchant is trying to promote.**\n\n**Answer: D**",
