      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which statement is a rebuttal to the given context. Let me read the context again carefully.\n\nThe context says that people can be divided into two classes: those who are ambitious and those who aren't. For ordinary people, a little ambition is a strong motivation to get out of their ordinary lives. Without it, they can be powerless and submerged by ordinary life. In times of change, a little ambition can lead to big results.\n\nSo the statement in the context is about the importance of ambition for ordinary people. The question is asking which option is a rebuttal to this statement. A rebuttal would likely challenge the idea that ambition is necessary or that it's not enough.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) Liu bei... never forgot that he was the emperor's uncle. Because of this, he went from empty-handed to one-third of the world. This seems like a positive example, showing that ambition can lead to significant achievements. It's not a rebuttal but more of a support.\n\nB) Zhang xiong had high ambitions but was mediocre in intelligence. He worked hard but nothing was accomplished. He was bruised and hurt. This seems like a counterexample to the idea that ambition alone is enough. It shows that even with ambition, if intelligence isn't strong, it might not lead to success. This could be a rebuttal because it challenges the assumption that ambition is sufficient.\n\nC) Liu qin has neither ambition nor special talent, but she has achieved many things. This seems like it's supporting the idea that without ambition, people can still succeed. It's not a rebuttal but more of an example of people who don't need much ambition.\n\nD) The chrysanthemum elder sister is neither talented nor beautiful, but she thinks highly of herself, constantly talks about life, and leads a prosperous life. This seems like it's supporting the idea that people can succeed without being highly talented or beautiful. It's not a rebuttal but more of an example.\n\nSo, the context is saying that ambition is important for ordinary people. A rebuttal would be an example where even with ambition, it's not enough. Option B fits this because it shows that even with ambition, intelligence is needed, so it's not enough on its own.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is:\n\n**B) Although Zhang xiong had high ambitions, he was mediocre in intelligence. he worked hard all his life, but nothing was accomplished, and he was bruised and bruised all over.**\n\nThis statement challenges the idea that ambition alone is sufficient by showing that even with ambition, intelligence is necessary for success.",
